      "problem": "A player's height in a particular professional basketball league is normally distributed with a mean of $77$ inches and a standard deviation of $3.57$ inches.\nWhat is the probability that the height of a randomly selected player is more than $76$ inches but less than $78$ inches?\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.1\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5636\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5675\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5714\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.2\\,$</th>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6026\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6064\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6103\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.3\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6406\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6443\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6480\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.3\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3594\\